parameters.message:
=A rate confirmation came in but Dispatch v2 could not fully auto-process it, so it needs a quick manual check.

Load #: {{ $json.alert_load }}
Subject: {{ $json.alert_subject }}
From: {{ $json.alert_from }}
Received: {{ $json.alert_received }}

Why it stopped: {{ $json.alert_reason }}

WHAT TO DO
1. Open the "Job Tracking" sheet and search for the Load # above.
2. If the row EXISTS, the load was captured — just fill any blank cells. The most common gap is the Drop-off Address (some brokers put the delivery street on an "Address:" line under the receiver, with the city in the directions/notes).
3. If the row is MISSING, an earlier parse step failed — open the rate con PDF and enter the load manually, or drag the PDF onto the Job Board in LogisX to auto-fill it.
4. Check the row before re-entering anything to avoid a duplicate.

Details: n8n -> Dispatch v2 (Fixed) -> Executions -> #{{ $json.alert_execution }}.
(Automated alert. Reply not needed.)

